#: src/manpages.rs:300
msgid ""
"The sleep history comes from the system journal, which members of the adm or systemd-journal groups can read. Linux records what woke the computer only when it was the lid or the power button; other wakes are described by their likely causes. Which USB devices may wake the computer can be changed in the app (with the administrator password); the choice is kept in /etc/udev/rules.d/90-voltkit-wakeup.rules."
msgstr ""

#: src/manpages.rs:311
msgid ""
"The report leaves out serial numbers, user and computer names, and network addresses, so it can be posted in a forum or bug report. Drive health comes from UDisks2 and firmware updates from fwupd. Each run (and the background service, once a day) saves a snapshot of the hardware, drivers, kernel and firmware in ~/.local/share/voltkit/snapshots, which later reports compare to show what changed. --memory reads the memory slots from the SMBIOS tables, which needs the administrator password."
